<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mehrangarh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1459</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Mehrangarh Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mehrangarh is a fort above the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in 1459 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-jodha">Rao Jodha</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore dynasty</a> as the new capital of Marwar. Built on a steep rocky hill, it is one of the largest forts in India, with massive walls and palaces of carved sandstone added by later rulers, and now houses a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mehrangarh.jpg" alt="Mehrangarh" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sanhitasinha · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mehrangarh_Fort_sanhita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
